ISC Unix users may want to download the X11 nethack font to their
consoles. Now they can use the special nethack font without the
overhead of X11.

This is possible with only a small alteration.
Here is a context diff:

*** ibm.bdf	Wed Apr  1 16:46:21 1992
--- ibmisc.bdf	Mon Feb 22 17:00:49 1993
***************
*** 1,6 ****
  STARTFONT 2.1
  COMMENT (null)
! FONT -Misc-Fixed-Medium-R-Normal-IBMPC-14-120-75-75-C-80-ISO8859-1
  SIZE 13 78 78
  FONTBOUNDINGBOX 8 14 0 -3
  STARTPROPERTIES 19
--- 1,6 ----
  STARTFONT 2.1
  COMMENT (null)
! FONT 8x14
  SIZE 13 78 78
  FONTBOUNDINGBOX 8 14 0 -3
  STARTPROPERTIES 19

The 8x14 font can only be downloaded to an EGA, or a VGA in EGA
mode. I use the following script to accomplish the latter:


#!/bin/sh
set -e
# Go to EGA mode
loadfont -m E80x25
# download the font
loadfont -f /usr/local/src/games/nethack/win/X11/ibmisc.bdf
# set different options
NETHACKOPTIONS=$HOME/.nethack.egarc nethack $@
# make sure you can see the high score
read dummy
# before the screen is cleared by returning to VGA
loadfont -m V80x25

My .nethack.egarc sets the graphic characters as described
in win/X11/nethack.rc

Now if only someone would come up with an 8x16 font,
that can be downloaded in VGA mode.
